---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="How the three case studies were built, what they measure, and what the verification gate checks."
  ogImage="/og/home.png"
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Claims that a command can check.</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-body">
      <p>
        This site carries three case studies. Each starts with a claim that can
        fail and ends with the artifact and limits behind it. The e-commerce
        platform ran 20 concurrent checkouts against stock 5 and recorded 5
        orders, 15 rejections and stock 0. The pipeline feeds eight PR gates into
        one required ci-ok check, and its smoke gate rolled back a build whose
        POST /invoices returned 500; no Actions run exists, so red-PR blocking
        is not measured. DocQA scores recall@8 18/24 on its eval set, and three
        production gates fail in the committed report.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work on the parts that decide whether a system is correct:
        transaction boundaries, required checks, retrieval contracts. The
        choice of database or framework matters less than the invariant the
        system must hold, so each page names the invariant first and the tool
        second.
      </p>
      <p>
        The case pages are rebuilt from committed snapshots. <code>npm run
        verify</code> runs the type check, the asset and content contracts, the
        copy and accessibility audits, the JavaScript budget and a static
        build. When a cited artifact is missing, the build fails.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am looking for a team where correctness is a requirement and a
        failing test is a useful result. The <a href="/resume/">resume</a> and
        the <a href="/colophon/">colophon</a> carry the rest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
